Other LLM Scenarios the Platform Will Handle
•
Dispute intake: Customer calls to dispute a charge. The LLM reads the transcript in real time,
retrieves the transaction record and fraud score, and drafts a resolution recommendation for the
agent before the call ends.
•
•
Fraud ring briefing: When the graph detection engine flags a new cluster of suspicious accounts,
the LLM synthesises the graph data into a two-paragraph brief that an investigator can forward
directly to the fraud ring team or law enforcement liaison.
Regulatory explanation: When a model decision is challenged by a regulator or customer, the LLM
retrieves the SHAP values and drafts a plain-English explanation of exactly why the transaction
was scored as it was — satisfying SR 11-7 model explainability requirements.